Lab 4: Deploying and Operating the Control Plane
Objectives
Deploy OpenStack control plane services (Keystone, Glance, Nova, Neutron)
Monitor and verify control plane functionality
Configure access and roles for different users
Prerequisites
Ubuntu 22.04 LTS server with:
Minimum 8GB RAM
4 vCPUs
50GB disk space
Root/sudo access
Basic Linux command line knowledge
Internet connection
Lab Setup
Update system packages:
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
Install OpenStack client:
sudo apt install -y python3-openstackclient
Task 1: Install and Configure Control Plane Services
Subtask 1.1: Install and Configure Keystone (Identity Service)
Install Keystone packages:
sudo apt install -y keystone apache2 libapache2-mod-wsgi-py3
Configure Keystone database:
sudo mysql -e "CREATE DATABASE keystone"
sudo mysql -e "GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON keystone.* TO 'keystone'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'KEYSTONE_DBPASS'"
Edit Keystone configuration:
sudo vi /etc/keystone/keystone.conf
Add/modify these sections:

[database]
connection = mysql+pymysql://keystone:KEYSTONE_DBPASS@localhost/keystone

[token]
provider = fernet
Populate Keystone database:
sudo su -s /bin/sh -c "keystone-manage db_sync" keystone
Initialize Fernet keys:
sudo keystone-manage fernet_setup --keystone-user keystone --keystone-group keystone
Expected Outcome: Keystone service installed and database initialized.

Subtask 1.2: Install and Configure Glance (Image Service)
Install Glance packages:
sudo apt install -y glance
Configure Glance database:
sudo mysql -e "CREATE DATABASE glance"
sudo mysql -e "GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON glance.* TO 'glance'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'GLANCE_DBPASS'"
Edit Glance configuration:
sudo vi /etc/glance/glance-api.conf
Add/modify:

[database]
connection = mysql+pymysql://glance:GLANCE_DBPASS@localhost/glance

[keystone_authtoken]
www_authenticate_uri = http://localhost:5000
auth_url = http://localhost:5000
memcached_servers = localhost:11211
auth_type = password
project_domain_name = Default
user_domain_name = Default
project_name = service
username = glance
password = GLANCE_PASS

[paste_deploy]
flavor = keystone
Populate Glance database:
sudo su -s /bin/sh -c "glance-manage db_sync" glance
Expected Outcome: Glance service installed and ready for image management.

Subtask 1.3: Install and Configure Nova (Compute Service)
Install Nova packages:
sudo apt install -y nova-api nova-conductor nova-scheduler
Configure Nova database:
sudo mysql -e "CREATE DATABASE nova_api"
sudo mysql -e "CREATE DATABASE nova"
sudo mysql -e "GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON nova_api.* TO 'nova'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'NOVA_DBPASS'"
sudo mysql -e "GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON nova.* TO 'nova'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'NOVA_DBPASS'"
Edit Nova configuration:
sudo vi /etc/nova/nova.conf
Add/modify:

[api_database]
connection = mysql+pymysql://nova:NOVA_DBPASS@localhost/nova_api

[database]
connection = mysql+pymysql://nova:NOVA_DBPASS@localhost/nova

[api]
auth_strategy = keystone

[keystone_authtoken]
www_authenticate_uri = http://localhost:5000
auth_url = http://localhost:5000
memcached_servers = localhost:11211
auth_type = password
project_domain_name = Default
user_domain_name = Default
project_name = service
username = nova
password = NOVA_PASS
Populate Nova databases:
sudo su -s /bin/sh -c "nova-manage api_db sync" nova
sudo su -s /bin/sh -c "nova-manage db sync" nova
Expected Outcome: Nova services installed and ready to manage compute resources.

Task 2: Monitor and Verify Control Plane
Subtask 2.1: Verify Service Status
Check service status:
sudo systemctl list-units | grep -e keystone -e glance -e nova
Verify Keystone endpoint:
openstack catalog list
Check Glance functionality:
openstack image list
Expected Outcome: All services should show as active and respond to API calls.

Task 3: Configure Access and Roles
Subtask 3.1: Create Projects and Users
Create admin project:
openstack project create --domain default --description "Admin Project" admin
Create admin user:
openstack user create --domain default --password ADMIN_PASS admin
Create admin role:
openstack role create admin
Assign role to user:
openstack role add --project admin --user admin admin
Expected Outcome: New admin user created with proper privileges.

Conclusion
In this lab, you have:

Successfully deployed OpenStack control plane services (Keystone, Glance, Nova)
Verified the functionality of all services
Configured proper access control for administrative users
The control plane is now ready for further OpenStack deployment and management tasks.

Troubleshooting Tips
If services fail to start, check logs:
journalctl -u <service_name> -xe
Verify database connections if services don't respond
Ensure all passwords match between configuration files
Check firewall settings if API endpoints are inaccessible
